REFUSING: FABLE5_MODEL=4b has H=2560, which is NOT a power of two.
  The fixed-point normalizer (layer_fixed.rmsnorm_fx, mirroring
  rtl/vecnorm_unit.sv:277,323-325) produces N only by shifting
  `cfg_nlog2` and folds 1/N into the rsqrt binary point, so there
  is no representation for N=2560.
  This is docs/QWEN35_NEXT_FEASIBILITY.md §2.3 (wall 2): supporting it
  needs a reciprocal multiply in the normalizer datapath — an RTL
  decision on the layer critical path, not a host patch.
  Scoring it by normalizing over 2048 or 4096 instead would measure a
  machine nobody has proposed, so this harness refuses rather than guesses.
  (The float PPL ladder, ref/perplexity_eval.py, is unaffected: it uses
   the torch model's own normalizer and scores WEIGHT damage only.)
